Busy input steers the running turn (Nix, on top of compact-activity.patch).

Hermes One v0.7.8 held every message sent while the agent works in a
renderer-only queue (QueuedMessages above the composer) and submitted it
only after the turn's message.complete, as a new turn. The agent never saw
it during the turn, whatever its `display.busy_input_mode`; on a long turn
it sat there with a spinner for as long as the turn ran.

Now, like the official Hermes Desktop (use-busy-input-mode +
use-prompt-actions): a text message sent while a dashboard turn of this chat
is running reads the agent's policy (`config.get {key: "busy"}`) and
delivers it right away, `steer` -> `session.steer` (joins the turn after the
current tool step), `interrupt` -> `session.redirect`. Accepted: it appears
as a user message in the transcript, labelled "sent while working", and
nothing is queued. Only a refusal (mode `queue`, the turn ended meanwhile,
an approval/sudo or clarify prompt pending, as the official
busy-submit-state `canSteer`, attachments, a message already queued ahead,
no dashboard) keeps it in the local queue. A dropped socket is reattached
(session.resume) before steering. The drain now also runs when a message is
queued after the turn already ended (refused steer, slash `enqueuePrompt`),
so a queued message cannot be stranded. Busy sends are routed one at a time
in send order, so two quick sends across a turn end keep their order. A
refused steer whose chat was cleared or switched profile/connection
meanwhile is not queued into the other conversation: the submit fails, so
the words stay in the composer (or an error says it was not sent).

History: hermes stores a steer as a role=user row, display_kind "steer",
whose content is its model-facing "[OUT-OF-BAND USER MESSAGE …]" marker.
Both history loaders (state.db: sessions.ts expandRowsToHistory, dashboard
REST: remote-sessions.ts normalizeMessageRow) now show `display_content`
when the server sends it, else unwrap the marker of a steer row (hermes'
own _extract_steer_text_from_message rules), and flag the bubble
"sent while working".
Tested by src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/Chat.busy-steer.test.tsx,
src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useDashboardChatTransport.busy-steer.test.tsx
and src/main/sessions.steer-history.test.ts.

